AB  - The digitisation of sources has opened new perspectives for humanities scholars. Digitisation allowed a larger access to sources, removing some financial and geographical limits, and the use of digital tools provided new perspectives for humanities scholars, who are able to read the sources differently. However, working with digitised sources also created new challenges that humanities scholars are not always equipped to overcome.
